---
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import { SITE_TITLE, SITE_DESCRIPTION } from '../consts';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
	<BaseHead title={`Our Bread | ${SITE_TITLE}`} description={SITE_DESCRIPTION} />
</head>

<body>
	<Header />

	<main>
		<div class="article-hero">
			<div class="article-eyebrow">Flour. Water. Salt. Time.</div>
			<h1>Our Bread</h1>
			<p class="article-lead">
				Bread is one of humanity's oldest foods. Simple ingredients, yet together they create
				something extraordinary.
			</p>
		</div>

		<article class="article-body">
			<p>
				At Sonoran Rise Bakery, we believe exceptional bread begins long before the dough is
				mixed. It starts with thoughtfully grown grain, careful milling, and an understanding
				that great bread cannot be rushed. Every loaf is mixed, fermented, shaped, and baked
				with intention.
			</p>

			<p>
				We specialize in naturally leavened sourdough made with heritage and regionally
				inspired grains whenever possible. Long fermentation develops flavor, improves
				texture, and allows each loaf to express the character of the flour from which it
				was made.
			</p>

			<p class="pull-quote">We're interested in making bread worth slowing down for.</p>

			<div class="divider">
				<svg viewBox="0 0 120 30" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
					<line x1="8" y1="15" x2="112" y2="15" stroke="var(--accent-dark)" stroke-width="1.25"></line>
					<line x1="60" y1="15" x2="49" y2="4" stroke="var(--accent-dark)" stroke-width="1.5"></line>
					<line x1="60" y1="15" x2="71" y2="4" stroke="var(--accent-dark)" stroke-width="1.5"></line>
					<line x1="60" y1="15" x2="49" y2="26" stroke="var(--accent-dark)" stroke-width="1.5"></line>
					<line x1="60" y1="15" x2="71" y2="26" stroke="var(--accent-dark)" stroke-width="1.5"></line>
				</svg>
			</div>

			<h2>Our Philosophy</h2>

			<p>Good bread doesn't need a long list of ingredients &mdash; it needs good ingredients,
				careful hands, and patience.</p>

			<p>
				Our process favors time over shortcuts. Dough is allowed to ferment naturally,
				developing the complex flavors, open crumb, and crisp crust that define traditional
				artisan bread.
			</p>

			<p>
				Every loaf is shaped by hand. Every loaf is unique &mdash; and we believe those small
				differences are part of what makes handcrafted bread special.
			</p>

			<h2>Our Ingredients</h2>

			<p>We keep our ingredient list intentionally short.</p>

			<ul>
				<li>Flour</li>
				<li>Water</li>
				<li>Salt</li>
				<li>Natural sourdough starter</li>
			</ul>

			<p>
				Whenever possible, we seek out exceptional grains that tell the story of the people,
				culture, and region of the Sonoran Desert. We are especially passionate about
				heritage wheats and supporting the farmers, millers, and researchers preserving
				their remarkable flavors and histories &mdash; because great bread deserves great grain.
			</p>

			<h2>What You Can Expect</h2>

			<p>
				When you bring home a loaf from Sonoran Rise, we hope you'll notice more than its
				appearance.
			</p>

			<ul>
				<li>Smell the aroma released when the loaf is cut.</li>
				<li>Feel the texture of a well-developed crust.</li>
				<li>Slow down and enjoy the first bite.</li>
			</ul>

			<p>
				Bread has a way of bringing people together around a table, slowing down an
				otherwise busy day, and reminding us that simple things &mdash; made well &mdash; are
				often the most memorable.
			</p>

			<p class="pull-quote">That is the experience we strive to create with every loaf.</p>
		</article>
	</main>

	<Footer />
</body>
</html>
